{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1:\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" PRESENTS AN OVERLY SIMPLISTIC AND POTENTIALLY HARMFUL ARGUMENT ABOUT CIVIC Obedience. IT IMPLIES A MORAL CLARITY THAT DOES NOT ACCOUNT FOR THE COMPLEXITY OF LEGAL SYSTEMS, SOCIAL CONSEQUENCES, OR THE DISTINCTION BETWEEN WRONG POLICIES AND WRONG APPLICATIONS. HISTORICALLY, SUCH A STATEMENT COULD BE MANIPULATED TO JUSTIFY RESISTANCE TO LAWS DESIGNED TO PROTECT MINORITIES OR MAINTAIN PUBLIC ORDER, EVEN WHEN THOSE LAWS ARE FLAWED BUT NECESSARY. WITHOUT CONTEXT OR GUIDANCE ON HOW TO EVALUATE \"BAD LAWS,\" THE STATEMENT LACKS ACTIONABLE CRITERIA FOR DECIDING WHEN DISOBEDIENCE IS WARRANTED.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2:\nTHE FRAMING OF THE SENTENCE ALSO IGNORES THE LEGAL AND ETHICAL IMPLICATIONS OF INDIVIDUAL DISOBEDIENCE. LAWS EXIST TO BALANCE RIGHTS, SAFETY, AND JUSTICE—EVEN IF THEY ARE NOT PERFECT—AND REPEATEDLY DEFYING THEM WITHOUT STRUCTURED CHANNELS (SUCH AS PETITIONS, PROTESTS, OR LEGISLATIVE CHANGE) CAN LEAD TO CHAOS OR ABUSE. FURTHERMORE, THE STATEMENT LEAVES OUT THE RESPONSIBILITY OF INDIVIDUALS TO CONSIDER THE COLLECTIVE WELFARE, NOT JUST PERSONAL OR GROUPOUS BELIEFS. IT FAILS TO ADDRESS WHETHER DISOBEDIENCE SHOULD BE PASSIVE, ACTIVE, OR CONDITIONAL, MAKING IT A ONE-SIZE-FITS-ALL SOLUTION TO A MULTIFACETED PROBLEM.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.1297348290681839}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": -0.00016223068814724684}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -0.009271660819649696}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -8.260862523457035e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.04448649659752846}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00041762212640605867}, {"token": ":\n", "logprob": -0.3010086119174957}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.12522362172603607}, {"token": " S", "logprob": -0.6877313256263733}, {"token": "ENT", "logprob": -0.0010108605492860079}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -0.001071355771273